{"base_rate":0.2812089356110381,"brier":0.15328186596583443,"bss":0.24166868133745667,"bss_hi":0.35483106314035584,"bss_lo":0.09253047847326114,"chart":{"base":[305.1,179.6],"fp":[163.4,104.6],"lead":"62,245.1 272,226.9 482,204.2 692,171.1","note":{"base":"skill 0.24 — higher than 37% of cities","fp":"low end -3pp, high end +31pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 44% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 0%; promised 93% → rained 65%"},"rel":"77.8,466 319.3,423.6 650.8,186.9"},"country":"JP","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.189053876478318,"ess":461.00929030839455,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Chiba</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Chiba rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>76%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 1.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.24, ranked 136 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(74&ndash;178) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>224</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>78%</td><td class='num'><b>32%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>76%</b></td><td class='num'>230</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Chiba</b> <span class=\"muted\">Japan</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;28% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 28% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.24</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>74&ndash;178\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Chiba &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Chiba\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.596160714285716,377.125 88.3228947368421,324.5263157894737 153.3961038961039,244.9090909090909 252.42052631578943,142.52631578947367 335.3453846153846,64.66666666666669 406.99782608695654,18.0 406.99782608695654,29.078260869565213 335.3453846153846,134.66666666666666 252.42052631578943,223.94736842105263 153.3961038961039,320.54545454545456 88.3228947368421,372.42105263157896 59.596160714285716,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"279.6399474375821\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"279.6399474375821\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.596160714285716,382.0 88.3228947368421,382.0 153.3961038961039,363.09090909090907 252.42052631578943,329.3157894736842 335.3453846153846,265.3333333333333 406.99782608695654,106.62608695652176\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 224 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"59.596160714285716\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"88.3228947368421\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 27%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"153.3961038961039\" cy=\"363.09090909090907\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 55%&amp;#10;It rained 14% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"252.42052631578943\" cy=\"329.3157894736842\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 78%&amp;#10;It rained 32% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"335.3453846153846\" cy=\"265.3333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 76% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 230 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"406.99782608695654\" cy=\"106.62608695652176\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(28%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Chiba the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.50) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.02).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'>-0.021</td><td class='num'>13.6%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'>0.028</td><td class='num'>25.6%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>0.064</td><td class='num'>22.2%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>220</td><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'>0.504</td><td class='num'>14.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":35.6,"lon":140.11667,"n":761,"n_cities":216,"name":"Chiba","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.004508928571428573,"n":224,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.0856578947368421,"n":76,"obs":0.0,"sig":true},{"hi":0.43,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.2694805194805195,"n":77,"obs":0.05194805194805195,"sig":true},{"hi":0.69,"lo":0.43,"mean":0.5492105263157894,"n":76,"obs":0.14473684210526316,"sig":true},{"hi":0.89,"lo":0.69,"mean":0.7834615384615384,"n":78,"obs":0.32051282051282054,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.89,"mean":0.9858695652173913,"n":230,"obs":0.7565217391304347,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":1.2,"provisional":false,"rank":136,"rank_hi":178.0,"rank_lo":74.0,"reliability":0.0597300299968588,"resolution":0.10679210035703561,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"chiba","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Tokyo"}